# Signal Desktop — system floor. Users may tighten this, never loosen it.
#
# This applies to a NATIVE launch through cicada-run. A Flatpak install (the
# only supported path today — no official Arch package, and the AUR is out of
# scope) runs under Flatpak's own bwrap instead; `cicada-comms harden` is what
# tightens that one. docs/COMMS.md says which is in force and why.
#
# FILES=portal, not allow: the home the app sees is a tmpfs, and cicada-run
# binds back exactly one directory for this app id plus Downloads. Everything
# else — Documents, Pictures, the other profiles — is simply not there.
# MIC=deny is the default because a messenger that can hear the room whenever
# it likes is a bug the app cannot fix. Voice calls need MIC=allow — one toggle
# in Settings → App permissions, and deny looks like an unplugged mic, not a
# crash.
NETWORK=allow
FILES=portal
CAMERA=deny
MIC=deny
USB=deny
SENSORS=deny
